**v12 (Codex rA2 HIGH 1/2):** rc 7 is emitted by ONE function (`gpu_refuse`) and an EXIT trap remaps any other exit 7 — `train.py`'s own status included — to the terminal **rc 8**, so a trainer failure is never retried; after the gate the co-tenancy disclosure issues NO further nvidia-smi query (it prints the strict gate's validated answers: free MiB + uuid per card, compute processes on other cards). **v14 (SHARED-GPU launch mode, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25 ≈ 22:40 EDT — verbatim "please launch exp_25 if we have enough GPU free usage", then the AskUserQuestion choice "Relax the gates and launch shared now"):** the gate is MEMORY-ONLY: pinned `MIN_GPU_FREE_MIB=12288` (12 GiB per card; measured need of the identical `--batch-size 32 --num-gpus 2` recipe on this box: 5.9–6.6 GiB per rank in exp_14's smoke, ≈ 10.3 GiB per card for the exp_13 vanilla-B arm; the old 22.5 GiB floor was a margin, never a measurement), pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` (the other value, `idle`, restores the v10 refusal), the strict nvidia-smi parsing of v11 kept in full; foreign compute processes on GPU 0/1 are DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd) in the launch log and in the SMOKE evidence (`gpu_policy`, `min_gpu_free_mib`, `free_mib_at_launch`, `co_tenants_at_launch`) instead of refused; rc 7 stays reserved for the memory floor and unclean queries. Consequences carried as result disclosures: the FULL run and the campaign execute next to Yixun's xRIR exp_13/exp_28 chains (32 GiB each, 100 % utilization) and user dzheng's lanes — speed only, never the numbers; OOM risk in both directions (a co-tenant growing past the free memory kills whichever process allocates last; this launcher still never signals anything); the watcher's poll predicate mirrors the policy (foreign processes logged, memory floor decides). The eval campaign runs its lanes with `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (A6 opt-in, exercised by this instruction). Launcher exit codes: 0 ok · 2 a gate refused · 3 banner missing · 4 non-finite / SMOKE verdict FAILED · 5 checkpoint set wrong · 6 endpoint or two-rank start missing · 7 GPU gate (transient) · 8 a remapped 7 · anything else = `train.py`'s own status; (9) the interpreter is **enforced** (`command -v python` must resolve under `envs/flac/bin`; HIGH 6); (10) **tie-audit gate (BLOCKING 1; v11 = Codex rA A1 + rB B1):** SMOKE and FULL both refuse unless the committed, PINNED rung-3 audit report `depth_canon_tie_audit.json` + `.sha256` (in the pin set, committed at HEAD) passes THE one predicate `depth_canon_audit_gate.py` (`validate_tie_audit(audit_path, repo_root) -> (ok, problems, summary)`; CLI 0/1/2): sidecar, type-strict schema, `verdict PASS`, zero survivors/errors, full non-`--limit` coverage of the three splits, registered item counts, `dirty_code == ""`, no harness tag in production, the expected 9,650 unique map paths derived from the split JSONs through the audit script's own enumeration (path-set equality, no duplicates, typed rows), per-split census consistent with the rows, content hashes of the audit script / operator / `dataset.py` / `AR_md.py` / dataset configs / split JSONs, and a **re-hash of every current depth map** against the row hashes (8 threads inside a KILLABLE child process — the gate itself in `--rehash-worker` mode, own session — under the registered **900 s** wall-clock deadline `REHASH_DEADLINE_S`, no CLI or env override; read-only NAS, ≈ 2 min 15 s per launch; a timeout SIGKILLs the child's process group and fails closed, as do a nonzero child, no JSON or a malformed answer → launcher rc 2 → watcher FAILED; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 4). The gate module's sha256 joins the SMOKE→FULL content bind. Harness mode accepts a harness-tagged synthetic report only under `DEPTH_CANON_HARNESS` against a harness-provided contract file; (11) **SMOKE evidence (BLOCKING 2):** mandatory parsed finite loss and the wrapper's rank-0 fit-end line `canonicalize latency rank0 batches=<int> samples=<int> total_s=<float> mean_ms_per_batch=<float>` (no `null` fields); (12) the SMOKE→FULL bind is **content-scoped** (NIT): FULL requires the smoke's pin-manifest sha256 and training-closure content to equal the current tree's, so record-only commits between SMOKE and FULL are safe, while `EXPECT_HEAD` stays HEAD-identity for the launch itself (hence the freeze rule in §11 A5). Pin closure adds `FLAC_AR_BV.json` / `FLAC_AR_BF.json` (opened by the DINOv3 gate; HIGH 5) and, in v11, the committed tie-audit report + sidecar → **48 entries**; `assert_arm_configs.py::assert_vit_pin` now hash-pins the whole DINOv3 snapshot file set incl. `config.json` (Codex rA H5). W&B writes a repo-local `wandb/` directory (gitignored) — documented, not a gate. MODE=SMOKE (25 steps, cadence 10⁶ ⇒ no checkpoint, own namespace) → MODE=FULL requires a passing SMOKE on record. Guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` drives the launcher's real branches with `DRY_RUN=1` and synthetic logs in `mktemp -d` — never the production evidence directory.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_01-08-27_codex_code_rC_review.log:321:worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:133:**v10 (round 3c as built).** Cells are data: `depth_canon_cells.json` (230 rows = T 10, T-dup 2, C4+45 8, R 10, D-i 2, D-ii 2, S 10, P1-pin 28, YAW-pin 38, TRAJ 120; generated by `depth_canon_make_cells.py`, names injective through `build_output_paths`; `--blocks` selects the required set so A1 is a switch, `--no-dump-blocks` implements A3; flags written out explicitly incl. `--batch-size 64 --device cuda` and `--rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg θ` on every fixed cell; YAW-pin uses `exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/FLAC_AR_YAWAUG.json`, byte-equal to the YAW checkpoint's embedded config). `depth_canon_eval_run.sh`: gates (lock, flac interpreter, **strict HEAD pin** `EXPECT_HEAD` = the campaign's one evaluator pin — kept strict by Planner decision: no commits on the branch during the ≈ 23 h campaign, records go to the FLAC checkout; committed-tree check; config pins; dump ROOT on the NAS share), checkpoints sha256-verified once per path against the NAS manifest and linked into a local farm `outputs_FLAC/exp25_depth_canon/<ARM>/` so metrics never land in `ar_40k_endpoints/`; two GPU lanes; the complete-and-verified resume predicate (marker + `depth_canon_collect.verify_cell`, which reads each dump once), quarantine of anything else, a required per-cell receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (checkpoint sha checked before the run, configs, argv, pin, lane, rc), TRAJ last. **Eval GPU policy (A6, landed in rB-F1):** a lane is used only when its card has ≥ 10 GiB free AND no foreign compute process (uuid-mapped, fail-closed queries, re-checked right before each spawn); `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (explicit opt-in by Yixun) relaxes the occupancy part only — **exercised for the whole exp_25 campaign by Yixun's 2026-10-25 shared-launch instruction (v14).** **v11 driver integrity (Codex rB B3/B4):** the relevant-tree content digest is taken at start, before every spawn and after every cell — any change is PIN DRIFT, exit 4, no further spawns, running cells finish; checkpoints are copied into a content-addressed verified cache `<farm>/.ckpt_cache/<sha>.ckpt` (hash while copying, 0444, atomic rename, free-space gate ≈ 14 GB) and hard-linked into the farm (an existing cache entry must satisfy the immutable contract — regular file, mode 0444, the source's size — and is fully re-hashed at staging AND immediately before EACH spawn; the post-run MEASURED sha256 goes into the receipt; r3c-style symlink farms are refused). **v12 (Codex rB2 B4):** `eval_FLAC.py` reads the checkpoint ONCE into memory, hashes that buffer and deserializes that same buffer (`torch.load(io.BytesIO(buf), map_location='cpu')`, arguments otherwise unchanged), recording `ckpt_sha256_loaded` + `ckpt_bytes_loaded` in every metrics record right after the base keys (records built without it stay byte-identical); `build_receipt` refuses unless loaded == measured == manifest sha and the loaded length == the driver's post-run `stat` (`--ckpt-bytes`); `verify_cell` requires record == receipt for both fields; `--nas-retention-audit` refuses `--dump-check receipt` (rB2 NIT). **Receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (A7, landed):** written only after the post-run full verification; carries the campaign/spawn/post digests, the checkpoint shas (expected + measured + loaded, with the loaded length), `artifact_sha256` of the metrics / `.stream.json` / `.canon.json`, and `dump_evidence` (verified dump manifest sha256, n, shape, dtype, waveform sha256, marker); `verify_cell(dump_check='receipt')` and `gen_model_comparison.py` validate OFFLINE from the committed files; `depth_canon_collect.py --nas-retention-audit` checks the bulk dumps separately. `depth_canon_collect.py`: `verify_cell` (protocol + B2 binding fields per cell class, manifest-level dump check), pairs by (arm, K, seed, step) with the `input_hash` proof, Tier 1 per-position hash equality + recomputed `canonical_depth_hash`, Tier 2 from the dumps via `depth_canon_stats`, Tier 3 (`Δ_C4`, 45° probe, seed-paired `Δ_R` on input_hash-equal pairs only), the table block (mean ± sd, item-weighted and per-scene), TRAJ grid, tie counts per cell and per split, `--partial` labels every heading PARTIAL and lists the missing cells; writes `depth_canon_results.{md,json}`. **Tier-2 control mapping (registered):** 45° → d64, 90° → d128, 180° → d256, 270° → d384, random → random; the pooled control p99 is the reference; matched-offset AND pooled rules plus the 1e-2 cap are all applied (fail-closed reading of "control p99"). The collector accepts as the Tier-2 reference **only** a probe artifact marked `registered: true` (run without `--diagnostic`, sidecar-verified, bound to the CANON@40k checkpoint sha); diagnostic probes are refused (Codex r3b HIGH 4; probe exit codes 0 registered PASS / 1 verdict FAIL / 2 refused / 6 diagnostic); **v11 (Codex rB B5):** a dirty tree is a registered deviation; the collector's `PROBE_CONTRACT` checks the evaluator pin == campaign pin, exact registered arguments, config + split hashes, load protocol, stream census, and renders `eps_cond = v; registered threshold 1e-05: PASS/FAIL` (missing / non-finite ε → artifact invalid). **Pairing (v11, Codex rB NIT):** `context_ids` has exactly K entries per item; strict uniqueness is NOT required because `AR_md` draws with replacement when a room has fewer than K other sources (520 of 6,337 unseen K = 8 targets; identical across the 11 exp_15 streams checked) — the registered rule is that every cell of one (split, K) repeats on the same targets; identical generative noise follows from the execution protocol (same arm/K/step/seed, batch size, census under the pinned evaluator), not from the hash preimage. The shared-map overlap count is derived from the validated audit and compared with the registered 1,093 items / 112 maps. `gen_model_comparison.py` gains the `exp25` contract (rows CANON / P1-pin / YAW-pin at the exp_25 pin, YAW-pin labelled re-measured; validation through `verify_cell`; a round = two-K pair at one pin); additive only.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_01-08-27_codex_code_rC_review.log:324:worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:188:9. **Recovery (v13; Yixun A8 + integrative review HIGH 2):** the launcher has NO gated resume MODE (P1 recipe: no `--ckpt-path`; FULL requires an empty namespace; the checkpoint-set gate assumes one launch marker), so an ad-hoc autonomous resume is NOT performed. If FULL crashes: prove no rank or launcher remains; preserve the namespace + logs; identify the latest complete 2,500-step boundary (bytes, sha256, length, step, parent launch marker, parent manifest); then resume ONLY through a reviewed path — preferably a `MODE=RESUME` launcher extension (TDD + guard cases + Codex review; built after FULL has launched, since the branch is frozen until then) or, if the crash precedes it, the six-step manual prescription kept in the FLAC-checkout HANDOFF (every pre-launch gate re-run by hand incl. the audit re-hash, NAS, W&B, DINO/init and strict two-GPU occupancy right before launch; the exact recipe with ONLY `--ckpt-path <verified boundary>` added, 40k endpoint / cadence / offline kept, a resume marker, a fresh W&B run id with the parent recorded; the same banner / both-rank / finite-loss / endpoint / tie-count / latency / checkpoint-ownership / exact-byte checks with tie + latency totals aggregated across legs; ONE explicit CANON lineage manifest — original hashes through boundary N, resumed hashes after N, no duplicate or foreign step, endpoint included — passed explicitly to the collector; full disclosure of crash, boundary, parent/child identities and the RNG/dataloader discontinuity). A resumed CANON arm remains a historical matched-recipe comparison (P1 itself resumed at 32.5k) but not a bit-identical trajectory pair.
