/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:3318: `test_depth_canon_tie_audit.py` (23, v10): survivor detection = the operator's fail-closed branch; AR_md-built cloud vs raw-file selector; dedupe by resolved path; `--limit` forbids PASS (rc 4); dtype/shape contract violations are row errors (rc 3), never PASS; exit precedence INCOMPLETE (3) > FAIL (1) > REFUSED_SUBSET (4) > PASS (0); determinism across worker counts. `test_depth_canon_cond_probe.py` (24): stage chain pinned to `evaluate_model`'s key-strip / EMA selection / sampler; `--diagnostic` vs `registered` tagging; ARE refusal. ``test_depth_canon_collect.py` / `test_depth_canon_eval_run.py` / `test_gen_model_comparison_depth_canon.py` (+ `test_gen_model_comparison_data_curve.py` extended)` (25): cells manifest, driver (lanes, lock, resume predicate, quarantine, TRAJ last), collector (verify_cell, pairs, Tiers 1–3, control mapping, registered-probe refusals, partial mode, overlap disclosure), generator `exp25` contract. `test_depth_canon_autolaunch.py` (26, round 3d; subprocess-driven with a fake `nvidia-smi` and a fake launcher under a /tmp harness): no/stale/mismatched token → WAITING_TOKEN and no launch; busy GPUs → WAITING_GPU with the foreign process logged; counter reset on a dirty poll; three clean polls → SMOKE then FULL with the right env → DONE; GPU-gate failure → retry path, then FAILED after 5; any other SMOKE failure → FAILED without FULL; FULL failure → FAILED(rc); `nvidia-smi` failure = dirty; a commit between arming and firing → refusal; second instance → exit 2; launcher override without harness → exit 2; non-flac interpreter → exit 2; atomic, valid state JSON after every phase.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:3334: 9. **Recovery (v13; Yixun A8 + integrative review HIGH 2):** the launcher has NO gated resume MODE (P1 recipe: no `--ckpt-path`; FULL requires an empty namespace; the checkpoint-set gate assumes one launch marker), so an ad-hoc autonomous resume is NOT performed. If FULL crashes: prove no rank or launcher remains; preserve the namespace + logs; identify the latest complete 2,500-step boundary (bytes, sha256, length, step, parent launch marker, parent manifest); then resume ONLY through a reviewed path — preferably a `MODE=RESUME` launcher extension (TDD + guard cases + Codex review; built after FULL has launched, since the branch is frozen until then) or, if the crash precedes it, the six-step manual prescription kept in the FLAC-checkout HANDOFF (every pre-launch gate re-run by hand incl. the audit re-hash, NAS, W&B, DINO/init and strict two-GPU occupancy right before launch; the exact recipe with ONLY `--ckpt-path <verified boundary>` added, 40k endpoint / cadence / offline kept, a resume marker, a fresh W&B run id with the parent recorded; the same banner / both-rank / finite-loss / endpoint / tie-count / latency / checkpoint-ownership / exact-byte checks with tie + latency totals aggregated across legs; ONE explicit CANON lineage manifest — original hashes through boundary N, resumed hashes after N, no duplicate or foreign step, endpoint included — passed explicitly to the collector; full disclosure of crash, boundary, parent/child identities and the RNG/dataloader discontinuity). A resumed CANON arm remains a historical matched-recipe comparison (P1 itself resumed at 32.5k) but not a bit-identical trajectory pair.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:3349: **`worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/`** — `FLAC_AR_CANON.json`; `depth_canon_launch.sh`; `depth_canon_guardtests.sh`; `depth_canon_pins.sha256` (manifest); `depth_canon_tie_audit.py`; `depth_canon_cond_probe.py`; `depth_canon_cells.json`; `depth_canon_eval_run.sh`; `depth_canon_collect.py`; `depth_canon_autolaunch.sh` (+ runtime `depth_canon_GO.token`, `depth_canon_autolaunch_state.json`, both untracked); `depth_canon_comparator_ledger.md`; `depth_canon_training_path_diff_audit.md`; plus the SOP artifacts.
