/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-26_06-19-22_codex_code_rC4_review.log:4328:   188	9. **Recovery (v13; Yixun A8 + integrative review HIGH 2):** the launcher has NO gated resume MODE (P1 recipe: no `--ckpt-path`; FULL requires an empty namespace; the checkpoint-set gate assumes one launch marker), so an ad-hoc autonomous resume is NOT performed. If FULL crashes: prove no rank or launcher remains; preserve the namespace + logs; identify the latest complete 2,500-step boundary (bytes, sha256, length, step, parent launch marker, parent manifest); then resume ONLY through a reviewed path — preferably a `MODE=RESUME` launcher extension (TDD + guard cases + Codex review; built after FULL has launched, since the branch is frozen until then) or, if the crash precedes it, the six-step manual prescription kept in the FLAC-checkout HANDOFF (every pre-launch gate re-run by hand incl. the audit re-hash, NAS, W&B, DINO/init and strict two-GPU occupancy right before launch; the exact recipe with ONLY `--ckpt-path <verified boundary>` added, 40k endpoint / cadence / offline kept, a resume marker, a fresh W&B run id with the parent recorded; the same banner / both-rank / finite-loss / endpoint / tie-count / latency / checkpoint-ownership / exact-byte checks with tie + latency totals aggregated across legs; ONE explicit CANON lineage manifest — original hashes through boundary N, resumed hashes after N, no duplicate or foreign step, endpoint included — passed explicitly to the collector; full disclosure of crash, boundary, parent/child identities and the RNG/dataloader discontinuity). A resumed CANON arm remains a historical matched-recipe comparison (P1 itself resumed at 32.5k) but not a bit-identical trajectory pair.
