/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:103:**Launcher `depth_canon_launch.sh`** — adapted from the reviewed exp_17 launcher with its r3 blocking findings applied AND the review-H9 gates: (1) reviewed-tree binding: pin **HEAD** and content-pin every file on the training path (`train.py`, `defaults.ini`, `src/data/*.py`, `src/models/*.py`, `src/training/*.py`, `src/inference/*.py`, `AR_md.py`, dataset config, split, VAE, control + arm config, the DINOv3 gate script) via a committed manifest; (2) smoke evidence must carry the same HEAD + manifest hash + `config contract OK`, and **a smoke is re-run after any review-driven source change**; (3) no `pipefail` around `tr | grep` — the log is read once into a variable after `wait`-draining the `tee` FIFO; (4) NaN/Inf check in FULL mode too; (5) **run-owned checkpoints**: FULL refuses a non-empty run namespace, every accepted checkpoint must be newer than the launch epoch, the cadence set must be exactly {2500, …, 40000}, foreign/stale files abort; (6) **NAS gate on the save filesystem**: mount identity (`findmnt`/`df` of the save path shows the CIFS share), a write-probe file, free space ≥ 30 GiB; (7) pinned smoke-projection threshold ≤ 60 h (**v14:** ≤ 120 h, because a shared card roughly halves the uncontended 0.259 opt-steps/s — the bound is a sanity cap on a co-tenant launch, not a speed target; **v15:** ≤ 300 h — SMOKE 2 (2026-10-26 05:38 EDT, `d838c8e`) measured the real contended rate next to two 100 %-utilization xRIR trainings: 19.27 s/step, ≈ 5× the uncontended 3.86 s/step, projected 214.1 h, so v14's 2× assumption was wrong by 2.5×; under `shared` the projection measures the co-tenants' load at that moment, which relaxes as they finish (their checkpoint cadence put GPU 0 free ≈ Oct 26 midday and GPU 1 ≈ Oct 27 05:00 EDT), so the cap keeps only its sanity role — 300 h ≈ 7× the uncontended 43 h still catches an order-of-magnitude pathology; the contended rate is disclosed in the evidence and the result tables as speed-only); **v10 (Codex r3b):** (8) GPU gate = ≥ 22.5 GiB free on BOTH cards **and zero foreign compute processes** on GPUs 0/1 (`nvidia-smi --query-compute-apps`; HIGH 7) — the launcher kills nothing; **v11:** every nvidia-smi query is strict (exit status checked apart from stdout, exactly one numeric memory row per card, malformed or unknown-uuid rows refuse) and every GPU-gate refusal exits with the DEDICATED **rc 7** (the watcher's only transient signal); **v12 (Codex rA2 HIGH 1/2):** rc 7 is emitted by ONE function (`gpu_refuse`) and an EXIT trap remaps any other exit 7 — `train.py`'s own status included — to the terminal **rc 8**, so a trainer failure is never retried; after the gate the co-tenancy disclosure issues NO further nvidia-smi query (it prints the strict gate's validated answers: free MiB + uuid per card, compute processes on other cards). **v14 (SHARED-GPU launch mode, ordered by Yixun 2026-10-25 ≈ 22:40 EDT — verbatim "please launch exp_25 if we have enough GPU free usage", then the AskUserQuestion choice "Relax the gates and launch shared now"):** the gate is MEMORY-ONLY: pinned `MIN_GPU_FREE_MIB=12288` (12 GiB per card; measured need of the identical `--batch-size 32 --num-gpus 2` recipe on this box: 5.9–6.6 GiB per rank in exp_14's smoke, ≈ 10.3 GiB per card for the exp_13 vanilla-B arm; the old 22.5 GiB floor was a margin, never a measurement), pinned `GPU_OCCUPANCY_POLICY=shared` (the other value, `idle`, restores the v10 refusal), the strict nvidia-smi parsing of v11 kept in full; foreign compute processes on GPU 0/1 are DISCLOSED (pid, card, used MiB, cwd) in the launch log and in the SMOKE evidence (`gpu_policy`, `min_gpu_free_mib`, `free_mib_at_launch`, `co_tenants_at_launch`) instead of refused; rc 7 stays reserved for the memory floor and unclean queries. Consequences carried as result disclosures: the FULL run and the campaign execute next to Yixun's xRIR exp_13/exp_28 chains (32 GiB each, 100 % utilization) and user dzheng's lanes — speed only, never the numbers; OOM risk in both directions (a co-tenant growing past the free memory kills whichever process allocates last; this launcher still never signals anything); the watcher's poll predicate mirrors the policy (foreign processes logged, memory floor decides). The eval campaign runs its lanes with `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (A6 opt-in, exercised by this instruction). Launcher exit codes: 0 ok · 2 a gate refused · 3 banner missing · 4 non-finite / SMOKE verdict FAILED · 5 checkpoint set wrong · 6 endpoint or two-rank start missing · 7 GPU gate (transient) · 8 a remapped 7 · anything else = `train.py`'s own status; (9) the interpreter is **enforced** (`command -v python` must resolve under `envs/flac/bin`; HIGH 6); (10) **tie-audit gate (BLOCKING 1; v11 = Codex rA A1 + rB B1):** SMOKE and FULL both refuse unless the committed, PINNED rung-3 audit report `depth_canon_tie_audit.json` + `.sha256` (in the pin set, committed at HEAD) passes THE one predicate `depth_canon_audit_gate.py` (`validate_tie_audit(audit_path, repo_root) -> (ok, problems, summary)`; CLI 0/1/2): sidecar, type-strict schema, `verdict PASS`, zero survivors/errors, full non-`--limit` coverage of the three splits, registered item counts, `dirty_code == ""`, no harness tag in production, the expected 9,650 unique map paths derived from the split JSONs through the audit script's own enumeration (path-set equality, no duplicates, typed rows), per-split census consistent with the rows, content hashes of the audit script / operator / `dataset.py` / `AR_md.py` / dataset configs / split JSONs, and a **re-hash of every current depth map** against the row hashes (8 threads inside a KILLABLE child process — the gate itself in `--rehash-worker` mode, own session — under the registered **900 s** wall-clock deadline `REHASH_DEADLINE_S`, no CLI or env override; read-only NAS, ≈ 2 min 15 s per launch; a timeout SIGKILLs the child's process group and fails closed, as do a nonzero child, no JSON or a malformed answer → launcher rc 2 → watcher FAILED; v12, Codex rA2 NIT 4). The gate module's sha256 joins the SMOKE→FULL content bind. Harness mode accepts a harness-tagged synthetic report only under `DEPTH_CANON_HARNESS` against a harness-provided contract file; (11) **SMOKE evidence (BLOCKING 2):** mandatory parsed finite loss and the wrapper's rank-0 fit-end line `canonicalize latency rank0 batches=<int> samples=<int> total_s=<float> mean_ms_per_batch=<float>` (no `null` fields); (12) the SMOKE→FULL bind is **content-scoped** (NIT): FULL requires the smoke's pin-manifest sha256 and training-closure content to equal the current tree's, so record-only commits between SMOKE and FULL are safe, while `EXPECT_HEAD` stays HEAD-identity for the launch itself (hence the freeze rule in §11 A5). Pin closure adds `FLAC_AR_BV.json` / `FLAC_AR_BF.json` (opened by the DINOv3 gate; HIGH 5) and, in v11, the committed tie-audit report + sidecar → **48 entries**; `assert_arm_configs.py::assert_vit_pin` now hash-pins the whole DINOv3 snapshot file set incl. `config.json` (Codex rA H5). W&B writes a repo-local `wandb/` directory (gitignored) — documented, not a gate. MODE=SMOKE (25 steps, cadence 10⁶ ⇒ no checkpoint, own namespace) → MODE=FULL requires a passing SMOKE on record. Guard suite `depth_canon_guardtests.sh` drives the launcher's real branches with `DRY_RUN=1` and synthetic logs in `mktemp -d` — never the production evidence directory.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:127:**Atomic cell completion (review r2 H3).** A cell now produces several required artifacts (metrics JSON, `.stream.json`, `.canon.json` when canonicalized, the waveform `.npy`, its `.sha256`, the manifest). `eval_FLAC.py` builds the waveform dump in a **same-filesystem staging directory** (`<final>.staging-<pid>`), verifies every artifact and checksum there, writes the `COMPLETE` marker **inside the staging directory last**, and only then atomically renames the already-complete directory to its final path (review r3 H2: a crash after the rename can no longer strand an unmarked, non-empty final directory). The driver's resume skips a cell **only** when the final directory carries the marker and the collector's verification of that cell passes; every final directory that fails the complete-and-verified predicate — unmarked, **or marker-bearing but collector-invalid** — and every leftover staging directory is quarantined (`<name>.incomplete-<ts>`) and reported before the cell is re-run. Tests simulate a crash immediately before and immediately after the rename. Dump directory names are derived from the metrics stem, so the filename injectivity test (§6 test 16) covers them too. **B-F** is NOT re-evaluated (fa eval ≈ 4×): it contributes its historical θ=0 row plus method-level A-F evidence only (no B-F@40k rotated cells exist) — the ledger below names every reused cell.
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:131:Drivers: `depth_canon_eval_run.sh` (adapted from exp_17's extras runner: shared lock, two GPUs round-robin, skip-if-exists resume, per-cell logs, completion count, cell classes as data) and `depth_canon_collect.py` (reads raw JSONs + `.stream.json` + `.canon.json` + waveform manifests; verifies every record's protocol fields against its cell class **including the B2 binding fields**; pairs cells by (K, seed) and asserts identical `input_hash`; Tier 1 hash equality; Tier 2 waveform statistics from the dumps; Tier 3 aggregates (item-weighted AND per-scene), `Δ_C4`, seed-paired `Δ_R`; writes `depth_canon_results.md`). A `gen_model_comparison.py` row spec for CANON, P1-pin and YAW-pin (announcement 04) lands with the first T results; the four-arm matched-A6000 table in `_results.md` uses only one-pin rows plus B-F's historical row, labelled as such (review H6).
/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/plan_depth_canon.md:133:**v10 (round 3c as built).** Cells are data: `depth_canon_cells.json` (230 rows = T 10, T-dup 2, C4+45 8, R 10, D-i 2, D-ii 2, S 10, P1-pin 28, YAW-pin 38, TRAJ 120; generated by `depth_canon_make_cells.py`, names injective through `build_output_paths`; `--blocks` selects the required set so A1 is a switch, `--no-dump-blocks` implements A3; flags written out explicitly incl. `--batch-size 64 --device cuda` and `--rotate-mode fixed --rotate-deg θ` on every fixed cell; YAW-pin uses `exp_15_yaw_aug_claude/FLAC_AR_YAWAUG.json`, byte-equal to the YAW checkpoint's embedded config). `depth_canon_eval_run.sh`: gates (lock, flac interpreter, **strict HEAD pin** `EXPECT_HEAD` = the campaign's one evaluator pin — kept strict by Planner decision: no commits on the branch during the ≈ 23 h campaign, records go to the FLAC checkout; committed-tree check; config pins; dump ROOT on the NAS share), checkpoints sha256-verified once per path against the NAS manifest and linked into a local farm `outputs_FLAC/exp25_depth_canon/<ARM>/` so metrics never land in `ar_40k_endpoints/`; two GPU lanes; the complete-and-verified resume predicate (marker + `depth_canon_collect.verify_cell`, which reads each dump once), quarantine of anything else, a required per-cell receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (checkpoint sha checked before the run, configs, argv, pin, lane, rc), TRAJ last. **Eval GPU policy (A6, landed in rB-F1):** a lane is used only when its card has ≥ 10 GiB free AND no foreign compute process (uuid-mapped, fail-closed queries, re-checked right before each spawn); `ALLOW_SHARED_GPU=1` (explicit opt-in by Yixun) relaxes the occupancy part only — **exercised for the whole exp_25 campaign by Yixun's 2026-10-25 shared-launch instruction (v14).** **v11 driver integrity (Codex rB B3/B4):** the relevant-tree content digest is taken at start, before every spawn and after every cell — any change is PIN DRIFT, exit 4, no further spawns, running cells finish; checkpoints are copied into a content-addressed verified cache `<farm>/.ckpt_cache/<sha>.ckpt` (hash while copying, 0444, atomic rename, free-space gate ≈ 14 GB) and hard-linked into the farm (an existing cache entry must satisfy the immutable contract — regular file, mode 0444, the source's size — and is fully re-hashed at staging AND immediately before EACH spawn; the post-run MEASURED sha256 goes into the receipt; r3c-style symlink farms are refused). **v12 (Codex rB2 B4):** `eval_FLAC.py` reads the checkpoint ONCE into memory, hashes that buffer and deserializes that same buffer (`torch.load(io.BytesIO(buf), map_location='cpu')`, arguments otherwise unchanged), recording `ckpt_sha256_loaded` + `ckpt_bytes_loaded` in every metrics record right after the base keys (records built without it stay byte-identical); `build_receipt` refuses unless loaded == measured == manifest sha and the loaded length == the driver's post-run `stat` (`--ckpt-bytes`); `verify_cell` requires record == receipt for both fields; `--nas-retention-audit` refuses `--dump-check receipt` (rB2 NIT). **Receipt `<stem>.cell.json` (A7, landed):** written only after the post-run full verification; carries the campaign/spawn/post digests, the checkpoint shas (expected + measured + loaded, with the loaded length), `artifact_sha256` of the metrics / `.stream.json` / `.canon.json`, and `dump_evidence` (verified dump manifest sha256, n, shape, dtype, waveform sha256, marker); `verify_cell(dump_check='receipt')` and `gen_model_comparison.py` validate OFFLINE from the committed files; `depth_canon_collect.py --nas-retention-audit` checks the bulk dumps separately. `depth_canon_collect.py`: `verify_cell` (protocol + B2 binding fields per cell class, manifest-level dump check), pairs by (arm, K, seed, step) with the `input_hash` proof, Tier 1 per-position hash equality + recomputed `canonical_depth_hash`, Tier 2 from the dumps via `depth_canon_stats`, Tier 3 (`Δ_C4`, 45° probe, seed-paired `Δ_R` on input_hash-equal pairs only), the table block (mean ± sd, item-weighted and per-scene), TRAJ grid, tie counts per cell and per split, `--partial` labels every heading PARTIAL and lists the missing cells; writes `depth_canon_results.{md,json}`. **Tier-2 control mapping (registered):** 45° → d64, 90° → d128, 180° → d256, 270° → d384, random → random; the pooled control p99 is the reference; matched-offset AND pooled rules plus the 1e-2 cap are all applied (fail-closed reading of "control p99"). The collector accepts as the Tier-2 reference **only** a probe artifact marked `registered: true` (run without `--diagnostic`, sidecar-verified, bound to the CANON@40k checkpoint sha); diagnostic probes are refused (Codex r3b HIGH 4; probe exit codes 0 registered PASS / 1 verdict FAIL / 2 refused / 6 diagnostic); **v11 (Codex rB B5):** a dirty tree is a registered deviation; the collector's `PROBE_CONTRACT` checks the evaluator pin == campaign pin, exact registered arguments, config + split hashes, load protocol, stream census, and renders `eps_cond = v; registered threshold 1e-05: PASS/FAIL` (missing / non-finite ε → artifact invalid). **Pairing (v11, Codex rB NIT):** `context_ids` has exactly K entries per item; strict uniqueness is NOT required because `AR_md` draws with replacement when a room has fewer than K other sources (520 of 6,337 unseen K = 8 targets; identical across the 11 exp_15 streams checked) — the registered rule is that every cell of one (split, K) repeats on the same targets; identical generative noise follows from the execution protocol (same arm/K/step/seed, batch size, census under the pinned evaluator), not from the hash preimage. The shared-map overlap count is derived from the validated audit and compared with the registered 1,093 items / 112 maps. `gen_model_comparison.py` gains the `exp25` contract (rows CANON / P1-pin / YAW-pin at the exp_25 pin, YAW-pin labelled re-measured; validation through `verify_cell`; a round = two-K pair at one pin); additive only.
