/home/yixunhu/codespace/exp-35-orbitrir-yaw/worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_25_depth_canon_claude/depth_canon_2026-10-23_16-40-44_codex_plan_review_r5.log:230:**Atomic cell completion (review r2 H3).** A cell now produces several required artifacts (metrics JSON, `.stream.json`, `.canon.json` when canonicalized, the waveform `.npy`, its `.sha256`, the manifest). `eval_FLAC.py` builds the waveform dump in a **same-filesystem staging directory** (`<final>.staging-<pid>`), verifies every artifact and checksum there, writes the `COMPLETE` marker **inside the staging directory last**, and only then atomically renames the already-complete directory to its final path (review r3 H2: a crash after the rename can no longer strand an unmarked, non-empty final directory). The driver's resume skips a cell **only** when the final directory carries the marker and the collector's verification of that cell passes; every final directory that fails the complete-and-verified predicate — unmarked, **or marker-bearing but collector-invalid** — and every leftover staging directory is quarantined (`<name>.incomplete-<ts>`) and reported before the cell is re-run. Tests simulate a crash immediately before and immediately after the rename. Dump directory names are derived from the metrics stem, so the filename injectivity test (§6 test 16) covers them too. **B-F** is NOT re-evaluated (fa eval ≈ 4×): it contributes its historical θ=0 row plus method-level A-F evidence only (no B-F@40k rotated cells exist) — the ledger below names every reused cell.
