worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_codex_planner_tooling_P3_review.md:11:The correct order is present: archive link, fsync `done/`, unlink active mark, fsync state directory at [records_txn.py:454–462](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:454). However, `os.unlink(manifest)` is outside the restoration `try`.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_codex_planner_tooling_P3_review.md:13:If an unlink wrapper performs the real unlink and then raises—or an asynchronous exception lands after the syscall took effect—the restoration block is never entered. The outer handler detects the missing mark and reports it at [records_txn.py:464–471](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:464), but the next transaction is not blocked. All destinations are installed and the `done/` archive exists, so this is less severe than P2’s partial-install blocker, but a reported failure followed by a rerun can duplicate non-idempotent appends.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_codex_planner_tooling_P3_review.md:15:The archive test makes unlink fail before calling the real operation at [test_records_txn.py:850–887](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/test_records_txn.py:850), so it cannot expose this window.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_codex_planner_tooling_P3_review.md:17:Fix: put both unlink and the state-directory fsync inside the restoration scope; if either raises and the active path is absent, restore it from `done/`. Add real-unlink-then-raise tests for `OSError` and `AsyncInterrupt`, plus a mutant moving unlink outside the protected scope.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_35_orbitrir_yaw_evidence_claude/orbitrir_yaw_evidence_codex_planner_tooling_P3_review.md:49:After successful debris cleanup, the active marker is unlinked at [records_txn.py:473–479](/tmp/claude-1007/-home-yixunhu-codespace-FLAC/1630c6fe-5d3e-42b4-94ec-1b6d3bcb0e4e/scratchpad/r3a/records_txn/records_txn.py:473), but the state directory is not fsynced. A crash can resurrect a stale marker. This is conservative rather than corrupting, but it falls short of the otherwise explicit durable lifecycle.
